      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "HOOKLINEANDSINKER (1) after racing in behind the leader at the bell finished fourth as the equal favourite last time out, beaten 7 metres, in a far better performance at this track over 2190m. No excuses from this advantageous draw. Meets a comparable field and he can take this out without surprising. OZZIE DAYBREAK (7) has been competitive of late and kept the ball rolling last time when 4.5 metres from the winner in third over 2190m at this track after getting checked in the early running. Should receive a soft trip on the inside of the second line but may need luck at some point. Good enough to win a race of this calibre. CALF PEN NZ (5) was out of the money two runs ago then broke and finished seventh last start over 2190m at this track, coming home 25 metres from the winner. Meets a similar line up so if he behaves a big run is likely. SHES POPPY (8) is heading the right way, improving last time out to finish third at this track over 2190m after she raced three-back on the fence.",
